{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Imglink: three mobile cart-drawer fixes that are all about TAP and
  SCROLL behaviour in #cart. Named for the first; the other two live here
  because overlay-group is at Shopify's hard limit of 25 sections and this is
  the drawer's interaction file.

  ================================================================
  1. TAPPING A CART ITEM'S PICTURE OPENS THAT PRODUCT'S PAGE.

  In the cart drawer each line item draws its thumbnail as

      <li> ... <figure><picture><img ...></picture></figure> ... </li>

  with NO anchor anywhere above the image -- the only link in the row is the
  product TITLE. On a phone that title is a small target sitting beside a big
  photo, and the photo is the thing shoppers actually tap, so tapping it did
  nothing and the row felt broken.

  WHY A DELEGATED LISTENER, NOT AN <a> WRAPPER. Wrapping the figure in an
  anchor would give real link semantics (long-press, open in new tab), but the
  theme replaces the drawer's contents wholesale on every add, remove and
  quantity change, and pg-cart-smooth's morph re-uses the surviving nodes. A
  wrapper would have to be re-applied after every one of those passes, and
  re-parenting nodes underneath the morph is exactly the kind of fight that
  produced the earlier upsell "spazzing". One listener bound once to the
  document, matched with closest(), survives every re-render without touching
  the DOM at all.

  THE CASE IS EXCLUDED, deliberately and by request. The R36S Protective Case
  ships as a free gift with the console, so its line in the cart is an outcome
  of the console purchase rather than something to go shopping for -- sending
  someone to its product page mid-cart is a detour, not a feature. It is matched
  on the product handle rather than on price or a "free" label, so the spare
  case (a real, paid variant of the same product) is excluded with it and a
  future change to the gift's price cannot silently switch the link back on.

  WHAT IT WILL NOT SWALLOW. The handler bails on anything that is already
  interactive -- the title link, the Remove and Undo links, the quantity
  steppers, any button, input or label -- so every existing control keeps its
  own behaviour. It also bails when the shopper is dragging out a text
  selection, and on anything but an unmodified primary click, so long-press and
  middle-click are left alone.

  Mobile only (760px, the same breakpoint the rest of the cart work uses), which
  is where the request came from; desktop rows are wider and the title link is
  an easy target there.
  ================================================================
  2. THE FREE-3rd-ORB CHOOSER OPENED WHERE NOBODY COULD SEE IT

  Reported as "it shows the option to add a 3rd free but when you do it doesn't
  let you select -- the selection drawer doesn't open". The drawer DOES open.
  Measured on a 390x844 phone with two orbs in the cart: tapping Add sets
  is-open on the row and .pg-unlock-pick becomes display:block, 137px tall, with
  its select inside. It is simply invisible.

  The reason is the pinned checkout pane. .sticky-in-panel is
  position:sticky, bottom:-34px, z-index:5 and painted solid white, 291px tall,
  and it sits across the bottom of the drawer. The offer row is in normal flow
  BEHIND it: measured, the row spans y=535..799 while the pane starts at y=553.
  So the moment the panel expands, the whole picker is behind an opaque panel.
  Nothing is broken -- it is covered.

  The fix is to scroll it out from under the pane rather than to paint it over
  the pane. Raising the row above z-index 5 would have put a dropdown on top of
  the CHECKOUT button, which trades one broken state for a worse one.

  So on open, the drawer's scroller is advanced by exactly the overlap plus a
  small margin, and only when there IS an overlap, so a chooser that already
  had room does not jump. It is done on a short timeout because the panel is
  built asynchronously (buildChooser resolves after a fetch), and re-checked
  once more a moment later in case the drawer re-rendered underneath it.

  ================================================================
  3. THE DEAD SCROLL AT THE BOTTOM, AND THE WHITE SPACE UNDER CHECKOUT

  Two measured faults, one cause each.

  THE FREEZE: the drawer's scrolling element reports scrollHeight 1392 against
  clientHeight 844 -- 548px of content it cannot reach, because assigning
  scrollTop to it does nothing (it reads back 0). With overscroll-behavior at
  its default of `auto`, dragging past that dead end CHAINS the gesture to the
  page behind the drawer, and iOS spends a beat rubber-banding the wrong
  element before it will accept an upward drag again. That is the "pane freezes
  and won't let you scroll back up for a second or two". `contain` keeps the
  gesture inside the drawer, so the dead end stops rather than bounces.

  THE WHITE SPACE UNDER CHECKOUT IS NOT FIXED, AND bottom:-34px IS NOT THE CAUSE.
  It looked like the obvious culprit, so it was tried: the pane is pinned with
  bottom:-34px, which reads like 34px of pane hanging off the bottom. Forcing it
  to 0 was measurably WORSE -- the pane's bottom edge moved from y=844 (flush
  with an 844px viewport) to y=810, opening a real 34px gap underneath it. The
  negative offset is load-bearing: it cancels a 34px offset the drawer applies
  further up, and with it removed the white space is created rather than closed.

  So that change is reverted and the pane is left exactly as the theme sets it.
  The trailing space reported on a phone is still unexplained -- it is not this
  property -- and rather than guess again at something that is visibly holding
  the layout together, it is left for a screenshot showing where the space
  actually appears. The freeze below IS fixed and was a separate fault.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* --- 3. see note above --- */
  /* .m6pn is a SIBLING of #cart, not a descendant -- measured: a `#cart .m6pn`
     rule matched nothing. Listed bare, and #cart kept for the drawer itself. */
  #cart,
  .m6pn,
  #cart .l4ca{
    overscroll-behavior:contain;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
  }
  @media (max-width:760px){
    /* make the picture read as tappable: a pointer, a suppressed grey iOS tap
       flash (the row supplies its own feedback below), and no long-press image
       callout, which otherwise offers "Save Image" instead of following it */
    #cart .l4ca li figure{
      cursor:pointer;
      -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;
      -webkit-touch-callout:none;
    }
    #cart .l4ca li figure img{pointer-events:none}
    /* a brief press state so the tap is acknowledged even before the page moves */
    #cart .l4ca li figure:active{opacity:.72;transition:opacity .06s ease}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgCartImgLink) return; window.pgCartImgLink = 1;

  /* Products whose picture is NOT a link. Matched on a handle FRAGMENT so the
     rule survives the handle being renamed around it (the case's handle carries
     a "-free-gift" suffix today). Both of the case's variants -- the free one
     and the paid spare -- share this handle, so both are covered. */
  var SKIP = ['r36s-protective-case'];

  function excluded(href){
    for (var i = 0; i < SKIP.length; i++){
      if (href.indexOf(SKIP[i]) > -1) return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  /* The row's own product link is the source of truth for where the picture
     should go: it is what the theme itself rendered for this line, so the
     picture can never point somewhere the row does not. */
  function hrefFor(li){
    var a = li.querySelector('a[href*="/products/"]');
    return a ? a.getAttribute('href') : '';
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (e.button !== 0 || e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey) return;
    if (!window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)').matches) return;

    var fig = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('#cart .l4ca li figure');
    if (!fig) return;

    /* never take a tap that belongs to a control that was already there */
    if (e.target.closest('a, button, input, select, textarea, label, [role="button"]')) return;

    /* a tap that ends a text selection is not a tap on the picture */
    var sel = window.getSelection && window.getSelection();
    if (sel && sel.type === 'Range' && String(sel).length) return;

    var li = fig.closest('li');
    if (!li) return;

    var href = hrefFor(li);
    if (!href || excluded(href)) return;

    e.preventDefault();
    window.location.href = href;
  }, true);

  /* ---- 2. bring the free-orb chooser out from behind the pinned pane ---- */
  function scroller(){
    var el = document.querySelector('#cart .l4ca');
    while (el && el !== document.body){
      var s = getComputedStyle(el);
      if (/auto|scroll/.test(s.overflowY) && el.scrollHeight > el.clientHeight + 4) return el;
      el = el.parentElement;
    }
    return document.querySelector('#cart .m6pn') || document.querySelector('.m6pn');
  }

  function reveal(){
    try {
      var pick = document.querySelector('#cart .pg-unlock.is-open .pg-unlock-pick');
      if (!pick) return;
      var pane = document.querySelector('#cart .sticky-in-panel');
      if (!pane) return;
      var pk = pick.getBoundingClientRect();
      var pn = pane.getBoundingClientRect();
      var over = pk.bottom - pn.top;          /* how far the picker runs under the pane */
      if (over <= 0) return;                  /* already clear: never jump for nothing */
      var sc = scroller();
      if (!sc) return;
      sc.scrollTop += over + 14;
    } catch(e){ /* a failed scroll must never break the cart */ }
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (!e.target.closest) return;
    if (!e.target.closest('.pg-unlock-add')) return;
    /* the panel is built after a fetch, so look once it can exist, then again
       in case the drawer re-rendered under it */
    setTimeout(reveal, 260);
    setTimeout(reveal, 900);
  }, true);
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
